        # ReleaseNotes of this module
        ReleaseNotes = @'
1.0.0
  - Converted from standalone Functions\Compress-Video.ps1 script into a
    Public\/Private\ module layout matching the other modules here.
  - Added GPU hardware acceleration support (NVENC/QSV/AMF) with 'Auto'
    detection via ffmpeg -encoders probing, falling back to CPU (libx265)
    if no hardware encoder is compiled in or requested explicitly.
  - Added ffprobe-based resume/skip detection: existing outputs are
    validated by comparing input/output durations within a configurable
    tolerance rather than just checking file existence, so interrupted
    runs never silently redo (or silently trust corrupt) work. Corrupt
    or duration-mismatched outputs are re-encoded (with a warning),
    never silently deleted.
  - Added throttled parallel execution via ForEach-Object -Parallel.
    Defaults to fully sequential (ThrottleLimit=1) for CPU encoding and
    2 for GPU encoding, always overridable via -ThrottleLimit, so the
    module never saturates the machine by default.
  - Every spawned ffmpeg process now runs at a reduced process priority
    (default BelowNormal, configurable) so compression never starves
    the interactive session.
  - Added persistent JSON configuration (Get-/Set-CompressVideoConfig)
    stored at $HOME\.config\Compress-Video\config.json, covering CRF,
    preset, audio settings, hardware acceleration, throttle limit,
    process priority, extensions, and resume tolerance.
'@

